      "body": "<!-- greptile_summary -->\n\n<h2><a href=\"https://app.greptile.com/api/retrigger?id=71561295\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/RetriggerDark.svg?v=2\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=2\"><img alt=\"Retrigger\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=2\" align=\"right\"></picture></a>Confidence Score: 5/5</h2>\n\n**[Medium risk]** Fixes attention window handling for FlashAttention 4\\.\n\nThe PR appears safe to merge; no actionable defect was established.\n\n<h3>Summary</h3>\n\nThe PR translates Transformer Engine’s unlimited-window sentinel to FA4’s `None` convention in standard and context-parallel attention.\n- Adds helper tests and a forced-FA4 causal forward/backward comparison against PyTorch SDPA.\n\n<!-- greptile_confidence_score:5 -->\n\n<sub>Reviews (1) · Last reviewed commit: [\"\\[PyTorch\\] Normalize FA4 unlimited attent...\"](https://github.com/nvidia/transformerengine/commit/96ff9f6be5496f0e5e2756afee5bb6902d171642)</sub>",
